        "ai_gen_block_05bfbfc_cqc7qG": {
          "type": "ai_gen_block_05bfbfc",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Frequently Asked Questions",
            "subtitle": "",
            "header_alignment": "center",
            "header_spacing": 30,
            "subtitle_spacing": 10,
            "question_1": " What Makes HIT IQ Different From A Traditional Electronic Scoring Target System?",
            "answer_1": "<p>HIT IQ is built as a live fire target system that uses thermal sensor hit detection, automated scoring, and wireless tablet control instead of relying solely on acoustic frames or wired legacy hardware. It integrates timing, hit factor metrics, and shooter data storage in one platform. The result is an electronic scoring target system tuned for modern military live fire training and law enforcement training on real ranges.</p>",
            "question_2": "Does HIT IQ Support Military Live Fire Training At Scale?",
            "answer_2": "<p>Yes. HIT IQ is purpose built for military live fire training environments where hundreds of rounds move across each lane daily. The self healing target surface minimizes change outs, and automated scoring with integrated timing keeps relays moving quickly. Combined with multi target control from one tablet, it is built to be the best scoring system for military ranges that need high throughput and objective results.</p>",
            "question_3": "How Does HIT IQ Improve Safety For Law Enforcement Training?",
            "answer_3": "<p>HIT IQ reduces the need for instructors or staff to travel downrange during law enforcement training events. Scoring, hit location, and timing are all visible from the tablet behind the line, so targets rarely need to be pasted or replaced during a session. That keeps personnel off the berm, simplifies control of the firing line, and supports safer law enforcement range training without sacrificing performance data.</p>",
            "question_4": " How Does Multi Target Control Impact Staffing And Range Operations?",
            "answer_4": "<p>Because one tablet can control and monitor multiple HIT IQ targets, instructors can manage several lanes or complex courses of fire from a single position. Strings can be started, stopped, and reset for the entire line without walking between targets. This reduces the number of staff required to run busy live fire events and lets existing personnel focus on supervision, safety, and coaching instead of manual scoring tasks.</p>",
            "question_5": "What Performance Data Does HIT IQ Capture And How Does It Support Readiness Reporting?",
            "answer_5": "<p>HIT IQ records hit location, timing, scores, misses, and hit factor style metrics for each shooter, then stores that information for later review. By turning live fire training targets with analytics into persistent records, commands can track trends across qualification and sustainment cycles, identify shooters who need remediation, and document that standards are being met. Exportable data supports readiness reporting and training documentation at multiple levels.</p>",
            "question_6": "How Does HIT IQ Set Up On Existing Ranges?",
            "answer_6": "<p>The system is modular and portable, built to mount on existing target stands or frames without trenching or permanent wiring. Instructors position the targets, power them up, and connect the control tablet over the wireless link. Courses of fire are selected in software and pushed to the targets. This approach lets organizations modernize scoring and data collection while keeping current range layouts and safety procedures largely unchanged.</p>",
            "question_7": "Does HIT IQ Support Mixed Pistol And Rifle Calibers On One Live Fire Target System?",
            "answer_7": "<p>Yes. HIT IQ is designed with all caliber detection capability for pistol and rifle rounds above its minimum velocity threshold, so mixed weapon evolutions can run on the same target surface. Agencies can transition from duty handgun to patrol rifle within a single session without changing hardware. That makes sustainment and qualification packages smoother for both military live fire training and law enforcement training programs.</p>",
            "question_8": "How Does HIT IQ Work With Simulators, VR, Or Weapon Mounted Smart Target System Tools?",
            "answer_8": "<p>HIT IQ is focused on live fire and complements rather than replaces simulators, VR judgemental systems, and weapon mounted analytics. Simulators are useful for decision making and de-escalation, while HIT IQ provides real recoil, blast, and ballistics with automation on the range. Many agencies pair dry fire or diagnostic smart target system tools for practice with HIT IQ for validation of standards under actual firing conditions.</p>",
            "question_9": "What Does The Demo And Quote Process Include For HIT IQ?",
            "answer_9": "<p>When you request a demo or pricing, DA Targets gathers information about your range configuration, lane count, training requirements, and current scoring process. The team then provides a live or virtual walkthrough of deploying the live fire target system, running representative drills, and reviewing analytics. Afterward you receive a tailored configuration and quote aligned with your training objectives, throughput goals, and procurement constraints, so decision makers can evaluate fit confidently.</p>",
            "question_10": "",
            "answer_10": "",
            "desktop_width_percent": 90,
